  "instructions": [
    "Rinse turkey necks and place them in a large pot with 2 cups of water; bring to a boil.",
    "Reduce heat to low and simmer the necks for 45 minutes, skimming off foam.",
    "Add diced onion, carrot, celery, minced garlic, cumin, coriander, salt, and pepper; continue simmering for 15 minutes.",
    "Remove necks, shred the meat, discard bones, and return shredded meat to pot.",
    "Stir in labneh and chopped mint; heat gently until the soup is hot but not boiling.",
    "Taste and adjust seasoning if needed.",
    "Serve hot, garnished with extra mint and a drizzle of olive oil.",
    "Ensure poultry is cooked to an internal temperature of 74°C / 165°F (juices run clear, no pink remaining) before serving."
